2276df48e536d00a61accd993a8","event_uuid":"0ffafd8b-0a9e-452f-aa4c-b292e0c26820","position":{"commit_sha":"4d9aa7183ec837f868f0d5afda38e0c244a8ec83","position":"1786181043505218001-0ffafd8b-0a9e-452f-aa4c-b292e0c26820"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e497205c82c1e6d6a5ae7f7ef110c6b66dacd0a8b2858644486fe59e5cb234e8","event_uuid":"e18d9476-ce9b-4064-a97b-650c3584fa48","position":{"commit_sha":"4d9aa7183ec837f868f0d5afda38e0c244a8ec83","position":"1786181044038482001-e18d9476-ce9b-4064-a97b-650c3584fa48"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786047092937110001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"82a79063-f86b-4410-8ff2-2c84bca5f98d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4fc1-dbde-6772-401f"}],"description":"Scope: `src/rebar/llm/**` excluding plan_review and workflow — the package root plus code_review, prompting, review_kernel, evals, criteria, overlap. ~218 lines leave.\n\nContains the repo's #1 hotspot: `runner.py` 797/800, 88 commits, 12 in five days, with a 371-line method at its C901 ceiling. Recovering ~45 lines takes headroom from 3 to ~48 — roughly 4-5 stories of runway WITHOUT another split. ADR 0056 measured prose at 40% of `run()` and 50% of its pre-call region.\n\nA self-contradicting module: THREE sites assert Anthropic 400s when extended thinking meets a native output constraint, while `structured.py:228-238` — 210 lines below one of them, in the same file — explicitly calls that 'a stale rationale' and 'a relic'.\n\nA dead field found via its own comment: `runner.py:94-97` says `extra_tools` 'is always None in practice'; grep confirms no caller sets it. Delete the field, not the comment.\n\nConfirmed exemplar for the maintainer's original finding: `capabilities.py:166-198` is structurally a complete ADR (security posture for a BLOCKING gate, three numbered bounds, an explicitly accepted limitation on domain controls) and NO ADR in the 83-file corpus mentions web search in any form.\n\n85 lines are free wins — history already citing b690, b300, 2682, 3a98, 7a79, e3cd, 8455. `providers.py:3-16` duplicates ADR 0059 §1 verbatim including its file:line citations.\n\ncapabilities.py:295-316 is a matrix that cost real AWS accounts to produce and says so; capabilities.py:269-281 carries a rejected-alternative warning sitting exactly where the next reader would reintroduce it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost; measured-fact and anti-refactor warnings stay verbatim\n## CORRECTION (plan defect + plan-review preempt, parent 373f disposition vocabulary)\n\nThe plan's `extra_tools` premise is FALSE and would cause a regression if executed literally.\n`extra_tools` is LIVE, not dead: `llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:469,665` set it (the\ntoken-recovery record tool, story 2948), `llm/workflow/runs.py` threads it end-to-end, and\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_banking.py:491` asserts `captured.get(\"extra_tools\")`\n(\"the record tool is still wired\"). The STALE unit is the `runner.py` comment claiming it \"is\nalways None in practice\" — that is CORRECTED in place; the field is DO_NOT_MOVE (load-bearing).\nSuperseding ACs below encode this and the 373f disposition rules.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above)\n\n- [ ] Every substantial in-scope comment unit is dispositioned into exactly one parent-373f\n      label: RELOCATE (to an ADR / docs / ticket, reduced to a one-line citation), DELETE, KEEP,\n      DO_NOT_MOVE, or CORRECT-IN-PLACE.\n- [ ] Decision rule CORRECT-vs-DELETE: a comment documenting CURRENT runtime behavior / a live\n      invariant is CORRECTED in place; a comment is DELETED only when the thing it describes no\n      longer exists (artifact removed, or superseded). Every DELETE records its reason\n      (referenced-artifact-gone / superseded) in the commit body or a ticket comment.\n- [ ] `runner.py` `extra_tools` field is KEPT (DO_NOT_MOVE — load-bearing via\n      completion_recovery/runs.py/tests); its stale \"always None in practice\" comment is\n      CORRECTED to reflect the story-2948 record-tool wiring (or deleted as superseded), with the\n      reason recorded. The field and its two call sites are NOT removed.\n- [ ] The three sites asserting an Anthropic-400 on extended-thinking + native-output-constraint\n      vs `structured.py:228-238` calling that rationale \"stale\"/\"a relic\" are RECONCILED\n      conservatively: determine which matches current runtime and CORRECT the stale side in\n      place; if the truth is not determinable from the code without behavior risk, KEEP both\n      verbatim (DO_NOT_MOVE) and file a `discovered_from` ticket rather than guess. No\n      load-bearing invariant is deleted on uncertainty.\n- [ ] The web-search capability security-posture block (`capabilities.py:166-198` — a structurally\n      complete ADR: BLOCKING-gate posture, three numbered bounds, an accepted limitation) is\n      RELOCATED into a NEW ADR with a unique unused number (>= 0063), which EXISTS and is\n      committed BEFORE the source comment is collapsed to a one-line citation.\n- [ ] Measured-fact and anti-refactor comments stay VERBATIM (DO_NOT_MOVE): the AWS-cost capability\n      matrix (`capabilities.py:295-316`) and the rejected-alternative warning\n      (`capabilities.py:269-281`). `providers.py:3-16` duplicating ADR 0059 §1 verbatim is\n      collapsed to a one-line citation.\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands;\n      lint/type pragmas (`# noqa`, `# type: ignore`, `# ruff:`, `# tickets-boundary-ok`) and\n      test-introspected docstrings are DO_NOT_MOVE.\n- [ ] The actual recovered comment-line count is measured (by diff) and recorded on this ticket\n      as an OUTPUT, not a target.\n- [ ] No behaviour change: the full test suite AND `make lint` / `make typecheck` pass unchanged.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","managed_refs":[["depends_on","4fc1-dbde-6772-401f"],["parent","373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf","parent_status_uuid":"0ffafd8b-0a9e-452f-aa4c-b292e0c26820","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"4b94-8734-b8f5-42b7","ticket_type":"task","title":"Comment triage: llm core","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5390da70-a241-445f-ac99-ffb0c584b5dc","82a79063-f86b-4410-8ff2-2c84bca5f98d","f9540182-3b58-47a1-806c-35ebbe2a9245","04fee7b6-1835-4e27-9903-49794b4d8fa5","0ffafd8b-0a9e-452f-aa4c-b292e0c26820","e18d9476-ce9b-4064-a97b-650c3584fa48"]},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786181044038482002,"uuid":"2ad21484-72fd-477b-a978-45aa248bfa3f"}